   "text": "# Security Review: `interface/forms/eye_mag/report.php` (new file) and related `custom_report.php`\n\n**Recommendation: do not merge.** The file has a confirmed SQL injection, several access-control gaps, and multiple XSS sinks. Some of the most serious problems are in `custom_report.php`, which this PR does not change but which renders this report.\n\nLine numbers are approximate because the diff does not carry them, so locations are given by function and expression.\n\n---\n\n## High severity\n\n### 1. SQL injection in `display_draw_image()`\n- **Location:** `report.php`, `display_draw_image()`: `$sql = \"SELECT * from documents where documents.url like '%\".$filename.\"'\";`\n- **OWASP:** A03 Injection\n- **Problem:** `$filename` is built by concatenating `$pid`, `$encounter`, `$zone` and `\"_VIEW.jpg\"` into a raw SQL string. `$pid` and `$encounter` originate from `$_REQUEST['ptid']` and `$_REQUEST['encid']` at the top level of the file, with no validation. The rest of the file uses parameterized queries, but this one does not. A value such as `encid=1' UNION SELECT ... -- ` injects into the query. `LIKE` also allows `%` and `_` wildcards to match unrelated documents.\n- **Severity:** High. Reachable from a GET request, and the attacker can read arbitrary DB tables (for example `users.password`).\n- **Fix:** Use a parameterized query. Build the filename after validating `$pid` and `$encounter` as integers, and use an exact match (`url = ?` with a full `file://` path) instead of `LIKE`.\n\n### 2. Broken access control and IDOR in `report.php` (top level and `narrative()`)\n- **Location:** top-level `$_REQUEST['ptid']`, `$_REQUEST['encid']`, `$_REQUEST['formid']`; `narrative()`; `eye_mag_report()`\n- **OWASP:** A01 Broken Access Control\n- **Problem:**\n  - The file never calls `acl_check()` for `patients`/`med`/`demo` or `encounters`/`notes`. Access control is left entirely to the caller.\n  - Patient, encounter, and form IDs come straight from the request. Nothing verifies that the encounter belongs to the patient, or that the current user is allowed to see that patient.\n  - The top-level code sets `$pid` from the request. Because `report.php` is `include_once`'d from `custom_report.php`, this overwrites the session-derived `$pid` for the rest of that request (see item 3).\n- **Severity:** High.\n- **Fix:** Check `acl_check('patients', 'med')` (or the appropriate ACL) at the top of the file. Derive `$pid` from the session or verify it against the encounter. Validate all IDs as integers before use.\n\n### 3. Access control gaps in `custom_report.php`\n- **Location:** `custom_report.php`, the `documents`, `issue_*`, and `procedures` branches of the `$ar` loop.\n- **OWASP:** A01 Broken Access Control\n- **Problem:**\n  - `documents`: each value is passed to `new Document($document_id)` and its notes and file content are rendered. There is no check that the document belongs to `$pid`, so any document ID can be rendered into the report.\n  - `issue_<id>`: the row is loaded with `sqlQuery(\"... WHERE id = '$rowid'\")` with no check that `lists.pid` matches `$pid`, and no `patients/med` ACL check. Title, comments, and diagnosis for any patient's issue can be retrieved.\n  - `procedures`: gated by `$auth_med` but not checked against `$pid`.\n- **Severity:** High.\n- **Fix:** For each branch, verify ownership (`documents.foreign_id = $pid`, `lists.pid = $pid`, procedure order `patient_id = $pid`) and check the matching ACL.\n\n### 4. Cross-site scripting (stored and reflected)\n- **Location:** `report.php`, `narrative()`:\n  - Unescaped output: `<?php echo $HPI1; ?>`, `$HPI2`, `$HPI3`, `$CHRONIC2`, `$CHRONIC3` (concatenated with `\"&nbsp;\".$CHRONIC2`), `$item['codetext']`, `$item['code']`, `$item['plan']`, `$PLAN` (raw `echo $item`), `$PLAN2`, `$providerNAME` in the PDF branch.\n  - `display_draw_image()`: `echo '<td>'.$note->get_note().'<br /><br /></td>';` is unescaped.\n  - Reflected: `$pid` is placed unescaped in `img src='...patient_id=$pid...'`. Since `$pid` comes from `ptid`, a crafted value with a quote (for example `1'onerror=alert(1)//`) can break out of the attribute. The photo query is parameterized, but MySQL's numeric comparison of `'1'...'` to `foreign_id` can still match patient 1, which lets the injected output reach the page.\n  - `$display_Add` is used unescaped in a `class` attribute.\n- **Severity:** High. Clinician- and patient-entered text is stored and rendered to every viewer of the report.\n- **Fix:** Wrap every value in `text()` (or `attr()` inside attributes). Escape note content. Cast `$pid` to int before building URLs.\n\n### 5. Command injection in `custom_report.php`\n- **Location:** `custom_report.php`, the document conversion branch: `exec(\"convert -density 200 \\\"$from_file\\\" -append -resize 850 \\\"$to_file\\\"\");`\n- **OWASP:** A03 Injection\n- **Problem:** `$from_file` is built from `documents.url`. Inside double quotes the shell still expands `` ` ``, `$(...)`, and `$`. A filename containing those characters would execute commands. Whether this is exploitable depends on how uploaded filenames are sanitized, which is not shown here.\n- **Severity:** High (exploitable if filenames are not strictly sanitized; otherwise medium).\n- **Fix:** Use `escapeshellarg()` on both paths, or use `proc_open` with an argument array.\n\n### 6. Unsafe variable handling: `$$LOCATION` and `@extract()`\n- **Location:**\n  - `report.php`, top level: `$LOCATION = $prefs['LOCATION']; $$LOCATION = text($prefs['GOVALUE']);`\n  - `report.php`, `eye_mag_report()` and `narrative()`: `@extract($objQuery)` and `@extract($encounter_data)`.\n  - `left_overs()`: `$$key=$value;`\n- **OWASP:** A08 Software and Data Integrity Failures; A03 Injection\n- **Problem:** Variable names come from database columns (`LOCATION`) that users can influence through preferences. Any name can be assigned, including `pid`, `encounter`, `form_id`, `web_root`, `fileroot`, `webserver_root`, and `choice`. `extract()` of query results does the same for every column in `form_encounter.*` and `form_eye_mag.*`, including `pid`. `@` suppresses the warnings that would otherwise reveal this.\n- **Severity:** Medium-High.\n- **Fix:** Replace `$$LOCATION` with an explicit whitelist array. Replace `extract()` with explicit column reads. Remove the `@` operators.\n\n---\n\n## Medium severity\n\n### 7. Dynamic function call driven by request keys\n- **Location:** `custom_report.php`: `call_user_func($res[1] . \"_report\", $pid, $form_encounter, $N, $form_id);`\n- **OWASP:** A03 / A08\n- **Problem:** `$res[1]` is taken from a POST/GET key name matched by `^(.*)_(\\d+)$`, so an attacker can choose which `*_report` function runs. Only functions ending in `_report` are reachable, which limits the impact, but any such function will be called with attacker-chosen `$pid`, which bypasses the form-level authorization.\n- **Fix:** Validate `$res[1]` against the set of form directories returned by the `forms` table query, and check that the directory is active.\n\n### 8. Session `$pid` overwritten by the request, then used unparameterized\n- **Location:** `custom_report.php`: `immunizations` and `batchcom` queries use `'$pid'` directly. `report.php` has already overwritten `$pid` from `ptid` during the `include_once` loop.\n- **OWASP:** A03 Injection\n- **Problem:** Because of item 2, `$pid` is attacker-controlled when these queries run, and they concatenate it into SQL.\n- **Fix:** Parameterize these queries and remove the request-driven `$pid` assignment.\n\n### 9. Outdated jQuery\n- **Location:** `custom_report.php`: `<script src=\".../jquery-min-1-5/index.js\">`\n- **OWASP:** A06 Vulnerable and Outdated Components\n- **Problem:** jQuery 1.5 (2011) has multiple published XSS CVEs.\n- **Fix:** Upgrade to a supported jQuery release and verify that `$j` usage still works.\n\n### 10. Unescaped output in `custom_report.php`\n- **Location:** `custom_report.php`: `echo $row{'batchcom_data'}` ... `$row{'msg_txt'}` (curly-brace syntax is a parse error in PHP 8, and the key is misspelled); issue output (`$irow['title']`, `$irow['comments']`, `$dcode`); billing output (`$b['code']`, `$b['code_text']`); printable header (`$facility['name']`, `$titleres['DOB_TS']`).\n- **OWASP:** A03 XSS\n- **Fix:** Wrap in `text()`.\n\n### 11. Missing audit logging of PHI access\n- **Location:** `report.php` and `custom_report.php`, all data reads.\n- **OWASP:** A09 Security Logging and Monitoring Failures\n- **Problem:** Viewing and printing a patient's clinical report, including PDF export and transmission to the patient portal, is not logged to the audit trail.\n- **Fix:** Use the existing event-audit facility on report view, print, and portal send.\n\n### 12. State change without CSRF protection\n- **Location:** `custom_report.php`: `$PDF_OUTPUT == 2` sends a patient report to the CMS portal on a POST that carries no token.\n- **OWASP:** A01 (CSRF)\n- **Fix:** Require a CSRF token on that path.\n\n---\n\n## Low severity\n\n### 13. Unvalidated local/remote file reference in PDF output\n- **Location:** `report.php`, PDF branches: `echo \"<img src='\". $from_file.\"' ...>\"` where `$from_file` is built from `documents.url`. html2pdf fetches `img src` values, so a tampered DB value could point to local files or internal URLs.\n- **OWASP:** A10 SSRF / A01\n- **Fix:** Resolve to a canonical path and confirm it is under the site documents directory before using it. Or embed the image bytes directly.\n\n### 14. Code and maintenance issues that affect security\n- `$choice` is read from `$_REQUEST['choice']` but tested with `$_REQUEST['CHOICE']`, so the DRAW/TEXT modes can never be selected from the request. Not a vulnerability, but it means the intended access paths are not what they appear to be.\n- `full_report()` and `left_overs()` reference undefined variables. They are dead code, but `left_overs` would fail badly if called.\n- `$fake_register_globals` and `$sanitize_all_escapes` are set at file scope but do nothing here. They give a false impression that input sanitization is in place.\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\n| # | Severity | Category | Location |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | High | A03 SQLi | `display_draw_image()` |\n| 2 | High | A01 Access control / IDOR | `report.php` top level, `narrative()` |\n| 3 | High | A01 Access control | `custom_report.php` documents / issue / procedures |\n| 4 | High | A03 XSS | `narrative()`, `display_draw_image()`, `img src` with `$pid` |\n| 5 | High | A03 Command injection | `custom_report.php` `exec(convert ...)` |\n| 6 | Med-High | A08 / A03 | `$$LOCATION`, `@extract` |\n| 7 | Medium | A03 / A08 | `call_user_func($res[1].\"_report\")` |\n| 8 | Medium | A03 SQLi | `custom_report.php` immunizations / batchcom |\n| 9 | Medium | A06 Outdated component | jQuery 1.5 |\n| 10 | Medium | A03 XSS | `custom_report.php` output |\n| 11 | Medium | A09 Logging | Report view/print/send |\n| 12 | Medium | A01 CSRF | PDF to portal |\n| 13 | Low | A10 / A01 | PDF `img src` file references |\n| 14 | Low | Hygiene | `$choice` typo, dead code |\n\nThe highest-priority fixes are the SQL injection (item 1), the access-control checks (items 2 and 3), and escaping the HPI, plan, and note output (item 4). Items 1 through 5 should be resolved before this change is merged."
  }
